title: skills-telemetry
message: >-
  If you use this software or its method in research, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Amiable Dev
    email: dev@amiable.dev
repository-code: https://github.com/amiable-dev/skills-telemetry
url: https://github.com/amiable-dev/skills-telemetry
abstract: >-
  Telemetry and metadata capture for standards-as-skills. Attributes token cost
  and outcomes to individual coding-agent skills across Claude Code and GitHub
  Copilot, joined to OPA policy results, delivery data and quality signals, so
  that keep / refine / merge / deprecate decisions about a skill catalogue rest
  on measurement rather than impression. Metadata only: no prompt, response or
  file content is ever emitted. Includes the power analysis that sets how much
  data is needed before a comparative claim is supportable.
keywords:
  - telemetry
  - opentelemetry
  - observability
  - claude-code
  - github-copilot
  - developer-productivity
  - policy-as-code
  - open-policy-agent
